  <bioghist id="48b537120d35e1200b1c118cce636ec7">
    <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
<p>The Ford Foundation's office in Hanoi, Vietnam operated from 1996 to 2009. It was responsible for overseeing grants for the countries of Vietnam and (starting in 1998) Thailand. These grants focused on such areas of work as international cooperation, poverty alleviation, sexuality and reproductive health, the social sciences, arts and culture, and education.</p><p>The Ford Foundation's programming for Vietnam was carried out through its Bangkok, Thailand office in the early 1990s until the Vietnamese Government issued the Foundation a license to set up an office in 1996. The Foundation then closed its Bangkok office in 1998 and transferred responsibility for Thailand programming to the Hanoi office. By the end of the Hanoi office's first five years in operation, the Foundation had supported 227 grants comprising $31.4 million in total for Vietnam programs (The Ford Foundation's Program in Vietnam - briefing material May 2002 Board of Trustees Meeting, Ford Foundation records, Catalogued Reports, Reports 13949-17726 (FA739F), Report 016668).</p><p>In 2009, the Ford Foundation closed its Hanoi office as well as its office in Moscow, Russia.</p>  </bioghist>
